      "descriptions": [
        "<b>The ELIXIR Beacon Network (EBN)</b> is a federated discovery platform that allows users to query distributed biomedical datasets (such as genomic and phenotypic data) through the GA4GH Beacon v2 protocol. Rather than centralising data, the service queries participating beacons in real time and returns aggregated results while preserving local data sovereignty. EBN brings value by facilitating standardized, privacy-preserving data discovery in a federated manner. It supports a seamless integration of Node-operated beacon servers and establishes a unified search layer for European biomedical data infrastructures. Sponsored by ELIXIR, the project brings together four partner institutions—the Centre for Genomic Regulation (CRG, Spain), the Barcelona Supercomputing Center (BSC, Spain), CSC – IT Center for Science (Finland), and the University of Zurich (UZH, Switzerland)—to build an interconnected ecosystem of Beacons that enables responsible sharing of genomic, phenotypic, and other data types. <br/><br/>The onboarding of new beacons is regulated by standardized governance and validation procedures. The service includes beacon registration, validation and monitoring, a public web interface and API for federated search, and a governance structure for decision-making. As EBN serves purely as a <b>data discovery service</b>, it does not entail storage of raw or individual-level data, data access management nor brokering, nor bioinformatic analysis or compute services."
      ],
      "fundingOrgs": [
